ings/call-transcripts/2019/08/08/essential-properties-realty-trust-inc-eprt-q2-2019.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2019 Q2","e":"eprt","d":"2019-08-08","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"We generally focus on doing that only when we can create value either through restructuring that lease with the tenant or having unique insight into the tenant performance or relationship there, but generally trying to find inefficiencies where we're getting paid an attractive risk-adjusted return.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/08/essential-properties-realty-trust-inc-eprt-q2-2019.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2019 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2020-03-02","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"…say, clearly, and if you think about our entertainment sector comprising bowling alleys and movie theaters and places where people congregate, if the pandemic spreads and people elect not to use those facilities, it's going to impact the profitability of our tenants and the magnitude of that…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/02/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2019 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2020-03-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"We seek to mitigate these risks through restructuring process which focuses on direct sale-leasebacks on our lease form with master lease provisions and contractual tenant reporting requirements.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/02/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2019 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2020-03-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"And listen, I'm surely addressing hypothetical scenarios here, but it could be a liquidation, it could be someone buying a portion of their company and assuming our lease with the lease amendment, or it could be a Chapter 11 restructuring.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/03/02/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2019-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2020-05-11","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"Breaking down the unresolved portion of April rent, AMC Theaters and Art Van Furniture represents 73% of this cohort.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2020-05-11","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"I would say in general, we're really comfortable with the theaters that we own and we were very selective in the theaters that we purchased over the last three, four years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2020-05-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anthony K. Dobkin","x":"G&A during the quarter was higher than usual, both on a reported basis and after backing out the non-recurring impact of employee severance expenses.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2020-05-11","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Anthony K. Dobkin","x":"Lastly, given the economic uncertainty caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, we are withdrawing our 2020 guidance.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/11/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q2","e":"eprt","d":"2020-08-06","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"As you can see in our disclosure the vast majorities of our deferrals in July are concentrated in industries that continue to face closures and utilization or capacity constraints, including theaters, fitness centers and casual and family dining.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/06/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q2","e":"eprt","d":"2020-08-06","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"As of quarter end, we had $6.6 million of deferred rent remaining for future periods, those remaining deferrals are concentrated in our theater, health and fitness, entertainment and casual and family dining industries.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/06/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q2-2020-earnings.aspx"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2020-11-05","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Peter Mavoides","x":"The remaining 6% of contractual cash rent is allocated as follows: 2.5% is non recognized rent deferrals, which is mostly attributable to our five movie theaters that are leased to AMC theaters, 2.5% is unresolved, which is mostly attributable to Town Sports and Ruby Tuesdays.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2020-11-05","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"Conversely, we expect our concentration in the casual and family dining, home furnishings, health and fitness and movie theaters continuing to decline.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q3-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2021-02-25","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"On a different note I would like to highlight our progress toward reducing exposures to the more challenged industries of casual and family dining, health & fitness, home furnishings and movie theaters.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2021-02-25","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"Conversely, we expect further reductions to the casual and family dining, health & fitness, home furnishings and movie theater industries.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2021-02-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"Yeah, I mean, listen, we have 237 tenants, and certainly some of them are on our watch list, and we're working to right-size those investments as you see in our disposition activity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2020 Q4","e":"eprt","d":"2021-02-25","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"Listen, this whole COVID pandemic in our view really accelerated the restructuring of weak tenants within the portfolio.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q4-2020-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2021-05-04","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"Conversely, we expect further reductions to the movie theatres and home furnishings.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cinema","r":"analyst","s":"Sheila McGrath","x":"And then, Gregg, I think mentioned that in the pipeline, there's more entertainment, assets, but you're not focusing on cinemas.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Gregg Seibert","x":"That said, future disposition activities should moderate to levels more consistent with our historical average, as much of COVID related restructuring is behind us.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2021-05-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Mavoides","x":"What you're seeing there is largely the impact of some of our advan restructuring leases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/04/essential-properties-realty-eprt-q1-2021-earnings/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q2","e":"eprt","d":"2021-07-29","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Mark E. Patten","x":"…greatest level of impact in most -- and longest level impact, I would say, clearly in the movie theaters, which everyone knows and understand, but also the gyms have been slow but have recovered and then the early childhood education guys are still kind of ramping back up to pre-pandemic…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/essential-properties-realty-trust-eprt-q2-2021-ear/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q2","e":"eprt","d":"2021-07-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"When coupling this positive outlook for the back half of 2021 with our strong second quarter performance and our current capital position, we are raising our 2021 guidance range for AFFO per share to $1.30 to $1.32.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/essential-properties-realty-trust-eprt-q2-2021-ear/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2021-11-02","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"…this quarter, these statistics remain negatively skewed for certain industries like movie theaters, early childhood education and health and fitness which face continued state level shutdowns and capacity restrictions well into the spring of 2021 in certain areas of the country. However,…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/essential-properties-realty-trust-eprt-q3-2021-ear/"},{"c":"EPRT 2021 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2021-11-02","l":"theater","r":"management","s":"Pete Mavoides","x":"…the industries where the business is solely revolved around, the real estate, clearly the movie theaters in the current environment, quick-serve restaurants should be kind of in that 2, 2-plus range. So there is a wide dispersion of coverage, but we certainly think that headline number is…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/02/essential-properties-realty-trust-eprt-q3-2021-ear/"},{"c":"EPRT 2026 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2026-04-23","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Peter M. Mavoides","x":"Obviously, if volatility persists, it is going to put some strain on the consumer, and that puts strain at the margins on the portfolio, but certainly nothing that is outsized or gives us pause, which is one of the drivers of raising guidance here on this call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/eprt-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"EPRT 2026 Q1","e":"eprt","d":"2026-04-23","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jay Kornreich","x":"You mentioned that volatility could cause some strain on the consumer, yet you still feel confident in the investment pipeline as you increased guidance to $1.3 billion at the midpoint.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/23/eprt-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"EPRT 2026 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2026-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Robert Max Jenkins","x":"Diminished competition from private players in a more restrictive middle market lending landscape, are factors contributing to our pricing power.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/22/essential-properties-eprt-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"EPRT 2026 Q3","e":"eprt","d":"2026-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Robert W. Salisbury","x":"So, you know, we would hope to continue to achieve good pricing power to widen that spread out over time.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/10/22/essential-properties-eprt-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[36,1,5219,0,0,0,3889,875],[37,1,5356,5,5,0,3916,983],[38,1,5218,0,0,0,3777,897],[39,1,4945,0,0,0,3952,636],[40,1,4700,1,1,0,3581,731],[41,1,6918,4,4,0,4971,1418],[42,1,4201,4,4,